00:34:08.699 --> 00:34:11.040
Regarding my Shiny question,
what I'm envisioning

00:34:11.040 --> 00:34:16.800
is a button in my Shiny app that
an end user can press that will

00:34:16.800 --> 00:34:21.690
output a PowerPoint, which will
contain an image of the graph

00:34:21.690 --> 00:34:24.840
that the end user
has customized.

00:34:24.840 --> 00:34:27.050
So here's the rule
of thumb with Shiny.

00:34:27.050 --> 00:34:30.314
You can do anything with Shiny.

00:34:30.314 --> 00:34:32.980
It's basically unbounded.

00:34:32.980 --> 00:34:35.460
So if you want to have
a Shiny application that

00:34:35.460 --> 00:34:38.159
renders a PowerPoint
presentation from a button

00:34:38.159 --> 00:34:41.370
press and then allows you to
download that or even pipe that

00:34:41.370 --> 00:34:44.429
to some other system,
you can do all of that.

00:34:44.429 --> 00:34:48.270
And you might use an R package
to render that PowerPoint

00:34:48.270 --> 00:34:52.320
presentation, or you
might use R Markdown file

00:34:52.320 --> 00:34:53.699
to render that presentation.

00:34:53.699 --> 00:34:56.290
It's really up to you to
determine how to do that.

00:34:56.290 --> 00:34:59.017
But if you use the
R Markdown format,

00:34:59.017 --> 00:35:00.600
you'll want to use
that render command

00:35:00.600 --> 00:35:06.540
that we showed you to generate
the PowerPoint output.

00:35:06.540 --> 00:35:10.020
Do custom templates need to
be stored someplace specific?

00:35:10.020 --> 00:35:11.910
No, you can reference
them from any location

00:35:11.910 --> 00:35:13.239
in the yaml header.

00:35:13.239 --> 00:35:15.030
Does it matter if you
create the PowerPoint

00:35:15.030 --> 00:35:17.970
on a Windows laptop or a Mac?

00:35:17.970 --> 00:35:23.850
Will the images work if you open
the PowerPoint in the other OS

00:35:23.850 --> 00:35:24.840
